{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1551460-spirit-courts","id":1551460,"title":"Spirit Courts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-04T08:38:33-07:00","id":1551460,"title":"Spirit Courts?","content":"Are there any example courts?<br /> <br /> I've read a bit in the Book of Spirits which suggests a Stag Spirit ruling the local forest ending up causing stag like qualities in the local tree spirits (presumably due to them feeding on stage like essence that he influences into existence?)<br /> <br /> But I find this rather confusing, and at odds with what I've read elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Like I would have assuming a higher rank spirit of domesticated dogs might have low rank dog spirits tithing them essence, and then a bigger domesticated animals spirit might get tithes from the one for domesticated dogs, above whom there is a more general animals spirit and so on. With the Animals spirit not caring so much whether it is wild animals or domesticated animals in the local area that are ultimately generating essence for it. So lig as it gets its due...<br /> <br /> My other questions are around how the courts work horizontally. Like does the Animals court interact with the elemental courts if the area? Or do the elemental courts and the human technology court have some deal to keep the electricity running even if it means fucking over the animals??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-04T13:30:40-07:00","id":1551464,"title":"","content":"All the spirits in an area form a court; the horizontal interaction you're talking about is the stuff of choirs/umia, which interact in whatever ways their attendant phenomena interact plus whatever local agreements and relationships are in play. The court is just whatever functional or dysfunctional collection of spirits operate within the area, with importance given to spirits powerful enough to be dissociated from a single specimen of their Flesh-side bases.<br /> <br /> Swift-Eyed Hart is an example given of how a domain works, in specific contrast to the more &quot;natural&quot; outcome of a brood. It should not be taken as the normal state of affairs for the Hisil, because stags do not normally exert that degree of influence over their surroundings \u2014 a domain is the result of conscious effort on the part of its ruling pantheon, as contrasted with a bunch of spirits of different types that happen to have compatible Essence profiles forming a brood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-04T18:38:13-07:00","id":1551466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1551460-spirit-courts?p=1551464#post1551464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the spirits in an area form a court; the horizontal interaction you're talking about is the stuff of choirs/umia, which interact in whatever ways their attendant phenomena interact plus whatever local agreements and relationships are in play. The court is just whatever functional or dysfunctional collection of spirits operate within the area, with importance given to spirits powerful enough to be dissociated from a single specimen of their Flesh-side bases.<br /> <br /> Swift-Eyed Hart is an example given of how a domain works, in specific contrast to the more &quot;natural&quot; outcome of a brood. It should not be taken as the normal state of affairs for the Hisil, because stags do not normally exert that degree of influence over their surroundings \u2014 a domain is the result of conscious effort on the part of its ruling pantheon, as contrasted with a bunch of spirits of different types that happen to have compatible Essence profiles forming a brood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so the Umia in a given area may be made up of broods which go around ecerting their influence to benefit each of the individual spirits, but the highest rank spirit isn't necessarily the head of the local court, directing all the other spirits in an area...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-04T19:13:32-07:00","id":1551467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1551460-spirit-courts?p=1551466#post1551466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so the Umia in a given area may be made up of broods which go around ecerting their influence to benefit each of the individual spirits, but the highest rank spirit isn't necessarily the head of the local court, directing all the other spirits in an area...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The spirit courts&quot; is often used as a broad term for spirits as a collective and interconnected whole, but domains, where one or more spirits are actively propagating one type of Essence over all others, are the product of directed political effort by spirits behaving as actors disproportionate to the natural functioning of the things that empower them. Per the Broods sidebar on page 182 of the 2e core, the spirits of a court answer to its most powerful member(s) by virtue of their strength and influence, but that doesn't imply an organization a la the feudal court structure of some domains.<br /> <br /> Umia are broad categories of type of spirit like (to use the lexicon's examples) weather spirits, wind spirit spirits, or storm spirits. They aren't usually an organized group except in terms of general affinity from shared origins \u2014 a spirit comes into being as part of a choir whether it means to or not. Broods are closer to packs in concept and tend to share a common theme or purpose relating to their members' needs, and they can arise organically. Ilthum are deliberately joined or formed by spirits of the same more particular conceptual basis in contrast with the broader inborn foldering of the umia.<br /> <br /> The spirit(s) at the top of a court will almost definitely have an umia (magath being shunned for having shifted their essential being outside of the natural order), and may be part of a brood and/or ilthum (either of which may include spirits that share an originating concept with them), but unless they're actively forcing the Essence of the area to more strongly express the resonances that empower them in particular, the population of the court will typically look more like their own entities, with greater commonality (in direct resemblance or complementary development) being found between spirits that spend more time in the same places and eating the same food. The top dogs won't necessarily take a slice of the pie from everyone in town, but the spirits of an area have a survivorship bias in favor of not making decisive enemies of powerful entities (singular or collective); even if you don't get your dinner from the riverbank, you know better than to be there when the gators come ashore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-05T23:37:16-07:00","id":1551492,"title":"","content":"In the first edition Werewolf book Territories, one of the example territories is The Organ Pipe Cactus National Monument, basically a huge patch of scrub, grass, and woodland at the edge of Arizona on the border to Mexico. A real place. It's notable because it's a place the spirit is at war between two spirit courts and the rising of a third. There's also very few werewolves there, mostly being in neighboring areas. One court is ruled by King Spine, a cactus spirit of Plants and Law, who its believed is backed by other, mysterious spirits. The newer Court of Lost Hopes is ruled by Garbed-in-Flesh-of-Shadows, a more powerful spirit (rank 4) of fear borne from the immigrants and drug smugglers who use the area to get into the US, and the border patrol who sometimes encounter them, rather than the nature of the land they're concerned with the human impact there. Lastly is the newcomer, Black Fire. Once a tiny campfire spirit it glut itself on some hidden loci it found and is now a beast at Rank 5. Still &quot;immature&quot; other spirits of fire and pain have sought it out to serve but it doesn't quite know what to do with them.<br /> <br /> The entire courts don't get character write-ups (there would be thousands), only the leaders. The 1e Predators book, though, is really one of the best guides for seeing the wide variety of spirit types there are. I thnk there's around a hundred different spirits written about there, from helions and lunes to different kinds of plants, buildings you might find in a city, and spirits of war and nightmares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-06-2025, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T03:37:57-07:00","id":1551711,"title":"","content":"Are there rules for Spirit gaining rank?<br /> <br /> Maybe this is a seperate topic, but I noticed the Ephemeral Cultist rules require the spending of XP and also &quot;devour essence related to their purview, usually by consuming similar spirits&quot;.<br /> <br /> So within a Spirit Court, is this the usual way to advance? Would high ranking members be using their influence to create resonance to then allow a new spirit to come into existence only for it to be eaten by some mid ranked spirit to fatten them up? Is there any clear rules around this? Or just vague, instances of individual spirits interacting with forsaken trying to get essence/spirits to feed on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T04:46:02-07:00","id":1551712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1551460-spirit-courts?p=1551711#post1551711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there rules for Spirit gaining rank?<br /> <br /> Maybe this is a seperate topic, but I noticed the Ephemeral Cultist rules require the spending of XP and also &quot;devour essence related to their purview, usually by consuming similar spirits&quot;.<br /> <br /> So within a Spirit Court, is this the usual way to advance?</div> </div> </div> </div>This has always been the narrative explanation for how spirits conventionally gain Rank, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would high ranking members be using their influence to create resonance to then allow a new spirit to come into existence only for it to be eaten by some mid ranked spirit to fatten them up? Is there any clear rules around this? Or just vague, instances of individual spirits interacting with forsaken trying to get essence/spirits to feed on? </div> </div> </div>There are not hard mechanics for how much Essence or how many spirits of what power are needed to increase a spirit's Rank, mainly because spirits are primarily NPCs and there are so many variables brought in by the nature of Essence and its resonance and politics more broadly.<br /> <br /> Spirits gain in Rank by gaining in significance to the world, and the main way they do that is by being in circumstances that produce the stuff that empowers them and being powerful enough (in whatever way suits their idiom) to capitalize on and propagate those circumstances. Magath can sometimes gain a big singular boost to their Rank that their subsequent ostracization removes most of the peripheral advantages of that primal authority, barring the type of proactive movements that might produce a domain (notably the most successful hybrids tend to be ones with a theme to their disparate components).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T05:00:09-07:00","id":1551713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1551460-spirit-courts?p=1551712#post1551712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has always been the narrative explanation for how spirits conventionally gain Rank, yes.<br /> <br /> There are not hard mechanics for how much Essence or how many spirits of what power are needed to increase a spirit's Rank, mainly because spirits are primarily NPCs and there are so many variables brought in by the nature of Essence and its resonance and politics more broadly.<br /> <br /> Spirits gain in Rank by gaining in significance to the world, and the main way they do that is by being in circumstances that produce the stuff that empowers them and being powerful enough (in whatever way suits their idiom) to capitalize on and propagate those circumstances. Magath can sometimes gain a big singular boost to their Rank that their subsequent ostracization removes most of the peripheral advantages of that primal authority, barring the type of proactive movements that might produce a domain (notably the most successful hybrids tend to be ones with a theme to their disparate components).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I am asking because I was looking at the PC rules for Ephemeral Cultists.<br /> <br /> I guess that is the only context in which a player will be playing a spirit. But on the context of this thread, you are saying a spirit court will settle/form at some level reflecting the world that exists in the other side of the Shadow, they will gain or change rank when the significance of the concepts they represent change within the world (for whatever reason) and that could mean extra significance of (say) dogs in the area creating more dog spirits and resonance which feeds up until eventually the top dog gains a rank?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T06:16:12-07:00","id":1551717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1551460-spirit-courts?p=1551713#post1551713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But on the context of this thread, you are saying a spirit court will settle/form at some level reflecting the world that exists in the other side of the Shadow, they will gain or change rank when the significance of the concepts they represent change within the world (for whatever reason) and that could mean extra significance of (say) dogs in the area creating more dog spirits and resonance which feeds up until eventually the top dog gains a rank?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the background radiation of a game of Werewolf that involves the Shadow, yes. Some packs will be more proactive in steering their surroundings to affect the courts, while others may be more reactive and stick to dealing with the circumstances currently empowering a given troublesome spirit, but the game has always been built around (or at least adjacent to) the spiritual consequences of events in the material world in this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}